{
  "$schema": "../../schema/incident.schema.json",
  "protocol": "The DAO",
  "name": "TheDAO splitDAO recursive-call drain",
  "summary": "TheDAO.splitDAO sent the caller's share of ether to its child DAO and then paid the caller's rewards through ManagedAccount.payOut before zeroing the caller's token balance. The attacker's contract re-entered splitDAO from that payout, so each recursion moved the same unburned share again, draining TheDAO into the attacker's child DAO over hundreds of transactions.",
  "targets": [
    {
      "address": "0xbb9bc244d798123fde783fcc1c72d3bb8c189413",
      "reset": {
        "kind": "deployment",
        "tx": "0xe9ebfecc2fa10100db51a4408d18193b3ac504584b51a4e55bdef1318f0a30f9"
      }
    }
  ],
  "loss": {
    "usd": 56072614.97,
    "assets": [
      {
        "symbol": "ETH",
        "amount": "3641694.241898506992612617",
        "usd": 56072614.97
      }
    ]
  },
  "refs": [
    "https://github.com/blockchainsllc/DAO/blob/982e3c242ee31dfed4c04db79ea9751ac3e98efb/DAO.sol",
    "https://blog.ethereum.org/2016/06/17/critical-update-re-dao-vulnerability",
    "https://hackingdistributed.com/2016/06/18/analysis-of-the-dao-exploit/",
    "https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-779"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Loss is TheDAO's ether moved into the attacker's child DAO 0x304a554a by the attacker's 488 recursive transactions, at the DefiLlama daily ETH price for the anchor day. The hard fork at block 1920000 moved it to WithdrawDAO; that later recovery does not reduce the loss.",
    "Other recursive splits are excluded as Robin Hood (WHG) rescues: WHG DAO 0xb1367076 and the child DAOs 0x84ef4b23, 0x4613f3bc and 0xf4c64518 were filled by the same group, and on ETC their ether went to the WHG refund key 0x59bc6123. Unattributed recursive splits after the attack total under 6,000 ETH and are left out."
  ],
